# Cloudflare Pages caps this file at 100 static + 100 dynamic rules and silently
# drops everything past that point — we overflowed it once and lost the whole
# SPA fallback block (which sits last, because prefix rewrites must lose to the
# exact rules above). Every rule here must therefore be something Pages cannot
# already do on its own:
#
#   - Pages resolves a request for /x to /x.html before it consults this file,
#     so prerendered pages need no rewrite rule (a "200!" rule is doubly dead:
#     the build validator rejects the "!" suffix too).
#   - Pages answers /x/ with a 308 to /x on its own, so trailing-slash rules
#     are only worth their line when the target differs from the stripped path
#     (i.e. a retired URL that must land on a different listing).
#
# sitemap.xml is served directly on this host by a Worker route
# (balancebiketoddler.com/sitemap.xml) — no redirect needed here.
/api/* https://store.balancebiketoddler.com/api/:splat 307

# Legacy guide slugs inherited from the import pipeline (renamed 2026-09-17).
/guides/beginner/kidspullalongwagons-b0cs2zykc4overview /guides/beginner/best-balance-bike-for-1-year-old 301
/guides/beginner/kidspullalongwagons-b0cs2zykc4image /guides/beginner/how-to-choose-the-perfect-baby-stroller 301
# Legacy news slug inherited from the same pipeline (renamed 2026-09-17). The old
# sitemap also advertised it under a slugified category (/news/newproduct/...),
# which the app never resolved, so only the well-formed variant needs a rule.
/news/new_product/kidspullalongwagons-b0cs2zykc4image /news/new_product/strider-bikes-kellys-juvenile-models 301

# App roots with no prerendered HTML of their own. Static rewrites, so they must
# stay above the dynamic prefix block below and above the generated block, so
# the rule budget cannot push them out of the file.
/compare /index.html 200!
/auth /index.html 200!
/search /index.html 200!
/evaluations /index.html 200!
/transparency /index.html 200!

# scripts/prerender-pages.ts injects the retired-URL 301 family immediately
# above this marker. They stay above the SPA block below so exact (static)
# matches always win over the prefix rewrites.
# --- generated: begin anchor ---

# SPA fallback, prefix-scoped on purpose. Do NOT replace this with
# `/* /index.html 200`: a global catch-all serves the homepage shell with HTTP
# 200 for every unknown path, including inbound junk such as /panties/*.php
# left behind by whoever owned this domain before us. `_redirects` supports
# only 301/302/303/307/308 redirects and 200 rewrites — there is no way to
# answer with a 404 here — so unknown roots must stay unmatched and fall
# through to public/404.html, which Pages serves with a real 404 status.
#
# The prefixes mirror the roots the client router actually resolves in
# src/App.tsx (resolveRouteState); anything outside them already renders an
# in-app "not found" view, so nothing is lost by 404ing at the edge.
/products/* /index.html 200
/reviews/* /index.html 200
/evaluations/* /index.html 200
/guides/* /index.html 200
/news/* /index.html 200
/transparency/* /index.html 200
/about/* /index.html 200
/compare/* /index.html 200
/auth/* /index.html 200
/search/* /index.html 200
